Running Bowtie2 
```bash
#!/bin/bash

# Define paths
input_dir="/mnt/e/NHCS/NHCSMS/raw_data"
output_dir="/mnt/e/NHCS/NHCSMS/cleaned_nonhost"
bowtie2_index="/mnt/e/NHCS/NHCSMS/bowtie2/GRCh38_noalt_as"
threads=8

mkdir -p "$output_dir"

# Loop through R1 files with "_1.fq" suffix
for r1 in "$input_dir"/*_1.fq; do
    base=$(basename "$r1" _1.fq)
    r2="$input_dir/${base}_2.fq"

    # Skip if already processed
    if [[ -f "$output_dir/${base}_cleaned_R1.fq" && -f "$output_dir/${base}_host_sorted.bam" ]]; then
        echo "⚠️ Skipping $base – already processed."
        continue
    fi

    echo "🚀 Running Bowtie2 for $base..."

    # Align to host genome
    bowtie2 -x "$bowtie2_index" \
        -1 "$r1" -2 "$r2" \
        --very-sensitive \
        --threads $threads \
        -S "$output_dir/${base}_host.sam"

    # Convert SAM to sorted BAM
    samtools view -bS "$output_dir/${base}_host.sam" | \
        samtools sort -o "$output_dir/${base}_host_sorted.bam"

    # Index BAM file
    samtools index "$output_dir/${base}_host_sorted.bam"

    # Extract unaligned paired reads (non-host)
    samtools fastq \
        -1 "$output_dir/${base}_cleaned_R1.fq" \
        -2 "$output_dir/${base}_cleaned_R2.fq" \
        -f 12 -F 256 "$output_dir/${base}_host_sorted.bam"

    echo "✅ Finished $base"
done

echo "🎉 All done."
```

Handles paired-end FASTQ, outputs: .sam/bam/bai/

Gene Prediction: MetaGeneMark
MetaGeneMark --> gmhmmp.out.faa(protein) +gmhmmp.out.fna(nucleotide)

Perform cluster redundant genes with CD-HIT
```bash
cd-hit -i gmhmmp.out.faa -o clustered_genes.faa -c 0.95 -n 5 -T 4 -M 16000
```
where: 
-c 0.95: 95% sequence identity threshold
-n 5: appropriate for 0.9-1.0 identity
Output: clustered_genes.faa +clustered_genes.faa.clstr
